# Automatic Picture in Picture of a window out of sight, the whole way: the window gives up key, macOS
# reports its occlusion, the window server says what is in front, and the video goes or stays.
# Another window over all of it sends a video playing sound to Picture in Picture, and it comes home
# when the window is key again (#117). A window with nothing in front keeps its video, and so does one
# that macOS calls not visible while only its own part is in front: on macOS 27.2.1 a window alone on
# a second display sent its video away when another app became active (#533). The child window here
# makes macOS 26 call the window not visible the same way.
# Needs the screen: a background test copy reports every window visible, so nothing here would run.
# promise: #533
requires screen
env CRA_TEST_BACKGROUND=0
budget rss=900 stalls50=40
pace 0.5

cra://open?url=${ORIGIN}/sound-video.html
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1
wait 1
cra://debug?cdp=Runtime.evaluate&params={"expression":"unmute()","userGesture":true,"awaitPromise":true}
expect-log Cra cdp Runtime.evaluate .*"value":"unmuted"
wait 3

# Nothing in front: a small window of Cra's beside it takes key.
cra://debug?coverWindow=aside
expect-log cover window: aside, this window not key
wait 3
reject-log enters Picture in Picture
cra://debug?coverWindow=off
wait 1

# Its own part over all of it: macOS calls it not visible, the window server shows nothing else (#533).
cra://debug?coverWindow=child
expect-log window not visible to macOS, nothing in front covers it: on screen, [0-9]+ in front \([1-9]
wait 2
reject-log enters Picture in Picture
cra://debug?coverWindow=off
wait 1

# Another window over all of it: out of sight, and back when the window is key again (#117).
cra://debug?coverWindow=other
expect-log enters Picture in Picture
cra://debug?coverWindow=off
expect-log leaves Picture in Picture
